 <p id="action-message" role="alert"></p><p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="landmass" class="legend" style="min-height:20px"></p><p class="legend"><label style="display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:6px"><input type="checkbox" id="rearOverlay"> Show rear exclusion strips (parallelPara)</label></p><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Site arrangement</h2><div id="map"></div><p class="legend"><span style="color:#13833d">● Activated (+)</span> · <span style="color:#d46a10">● Deactivated (−)</span> · <span style="color:#246ccc">● Pad adjusted (↕)</span> · Changes remain highlighted until the next action.</p><div id="changes" class="row" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="legend">Auto mode keeps the villa you activate and ghosts other villas as needed to satisfy the rules. Deactivation restores eligible ghosts. Manually deactivated villas stay off until explicitly activated or reset. With Auto mode off, all manual activations and deactivations are allowed; conflicts are shown without blocking the edit.<br>Hover for name · Click to toggle · Solid = active · Dashed = ghost · Red = active conflict</p></section>
 <section class="panel" id="inspector"><h2>Villa inspector</h2><div class="row"><select id="unit" aria-label="Selected villa"></select><button id="toggle"></button></div><p id="detail"></p><h2>View from the front façade</h2><div id="window"></div><p class="legend">Building silhouettes in angular coordinates. Dashed box: central view, symmetric about 0°. Ghosts do not obstruct. Partial-height obstruction counts proportionally.</p><div id="elevations"></div></section></div>
 <details class="panel" style="margin-top:22px"><summary>Calculation and assumptions</summary><p>Viewpoint: centre of the front façade, at pad level + eye height. Villas are solid vertical extrusions of their actual footprints. No fixed pad-drop threshold is used.</p><p>The horizontal window is ±15°. The central window is ±5° horizontally, from −2.5° to +2.5° vertically, centred on the 0° horizon. If the overall vertical window is narrower on either side, the central box shrinks equally on both sides to remain symmetric. The central requirement measures clear area, not a continuous opening. Default central blockage must be below 25%; exactly 25% fails.</p><p>Obstruction is measured as a fraction of horizontal-angle × vertical-angle area, with overlapping silhouettes counted once. Conservative 0.25° horizontal columns enclose each silhouette; narrow obstructions may be slightly overcounted. Pad fitting and removal use local search, not a maximum-count proof.</p><p>Defaults are study assumptions, not surveyed floor or roof heights. Eye height is measured from the pad; include any upper-floor offset here. Terrain, trees, windows and roof shape are not occluders in this building-only model. Terrain still supplies pad references and downhill orientation. Strict side clearance and existing geometry remain unchanged.</p><p><strong>Terrain editing:</strong> each contour line is simplified to at most 10 control points, which you can drag in the terrain panel. OK saves the edited lines and reports the landmass cut/fill against the shipped terrain — nothing else. <strong>Planar fitting</strong> then faces every uphill arrow downhill, rotates every long axis further than the perpendicular tolerance off the local contour normal onto it, and slides villas to repair the clearance and boundary conflicts that re-aiming disturbs; the downhill sense comes from the contour <em>levels</em> (an arrow may not oppose the direction of the nearest lower contour, which is what the elevation labels show), not from the interpolated field between lines. <strong>3D view fitting</strong> then adapts pads and activation for views. Elevation labels stay fixed; dragging a line never changes its labelled height.</p></details><div id="terrainPanel" hidden><div class="terrain-box"><div class="terrain-head"><h2>Edit terrain</h2><small class="muted">Drag the round control points (max 10 per line). Lines keep their labelled elevation.</small><span style="flex:1"></span><button id="terrainReset">Reset lines</button><button id="terrainCancel">Cancel</button><button id="terrainOk" class="primary">OK — save terrain</button></div><p id="terrainHint" class="legend">Selected line: none — click a line to select it. Drag points to reshape it.</p><div class="terrain-body"><div id="terrainSvg"></div></div></div></div><div id="terrainTip" class="terrain-tip" hidden></div><div id="hover" hidden></div></main>
